---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import ErrorBlock from "../components/ErrorBlock.astro";
import BenchTable from "../components/BenchTable.astro";
import StatusLists from "../components/StatusLists.astro";
import PineTexture from "../components/PineTexture.astro";
import Commands from "../components/Commands.astro";
import doodle from "../assets/images/pino_manga_doodle.png";

const raw = "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OGShawnLee/pino-lang/main";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Hero needles>
    <Fragment slot="title">A small, fast language for people <span class="poem">and for AI.</span></Fragment>
    <p slot="lead">
      No hidden sharing, no <code>null</code>, no garbage collector, and error messages written as plain sentences.
      Light enough to feel at home on a modest laptop.
    </p>
    <Fragment slot="links">
      <a href="/play/">Try it in your browser</a>
      <a class="quiet" href="/learn/">Read the guide</a>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <Section label="01 — Errors are values" id="errors">
    <Fragment slot="title">Handle the failure <span class="poem">right where it happens.</span></Fragment>
    <p class="text">
      A function that can fail returns a <code>Result</code>. <code>?</code> passes the failure up, and
      <code>or {"{ … }"}</code> handles it in place, with the error in <code>err</code> and <code>yield</code> giving
      the fallback value.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock name="divide" />
  </Section>

  <Section label="02 — Errors that read like sentences" id="messages">
    <Fragment slot="title">Errors that <span class="poem">help instead of scold.</span></Fragment>
    <ErrorBlock name="immutable" />
    <p class="note">
      There are no semicolons to forget. Nobody should fail a class over a missing semicolon. The checker saves its
      strictness for real mistakes, like changing data you said wouldn't change.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="03 — Values" id="values">
    <Fragment slot="title">Your data never changes <span class="poem">behind your back.</span></Fragment>
    <p class="text">
      In Python, JavaScript, Java or C#, giving a list to another variable or function hands over the
      <em>same</em> list, so a change on one side shows up on the other. In Pino, each side gets its own value. A function
      can change yours only if its parameter says <code>mut</code> and the call says <code>mut</code> too. It stays fast,
      because Pino only really copies when one side changes something.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock name="values" />
  </Section>

  <Section label="04 — Performance" id="performance">
    <Fragment slot="title">Compiled with <code>--release</code>, Pino runs in the same range as Go and Rust.</Fragment>
    <p class="text">
      The same algorithm in six languages, with checked output. <code>pino build --release</code> compiles through GCC
      or Clang; <code>pino run</code> uses the VM and needs no C compiler. The programs are small on purpose, so the
      fastest ones finish close to their startup time: the table shows they're in the same league, not which one wins.
      Building a string with <code>+</code> is still slow in native Pino; the fix is next.
    </p>
    <BenchTable
      caption="Benchmark times in milliseconds"
      rows={["fib", "binary-trees", "mandelbrot", "sort", "lexer", "string-build"]}
      columns={[
        { key: "pino-gcc", label: "Pino", pino: true },
        { key: "go", label: "Go" },
        { key: "rust", label: "Rust" },
        { key: "csharp", label: "C#" },
        { key: "bun", label: "Bun" },
        { key: "python", label: "Python" },
      ]}
    />
    <p class="more"><a href="/performance/">All results, with the VM and TinyCC builds</a></p>
  </Section>

  <section class="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
    <PineTexture place="section" />
    <div class="wrap inner">
      <p class="label">Status</p>
      <h2 id="status-title">Growing slowly,<br /><span class="poem">as a pine tree does.</span></h2>
      <StatusLists
        works={[
          "Pino 0.4 runs the whole language on a VM and as native C, with every conformance test passing on both.",
          "A complete written spec; every rule has tests.",
          "Plain-sentence errors, <code>pino test</code>, a REPL and a browser playground.",
        ]}
        notYet={[
          "Young, and a one-person project.",
          "A small standard library and no package ecosystem yet.",
          "No concurrency yet, and AI models know very little Pino.",
        ]}
      />
      <p class="more"><a href="/status/">Status and roadmap</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section label="Why it exists" id="why">
    <Fragment slot="title"><span class="visually-hidden">Why Pino exists</span></Fragment>
    <div class="why">
      <div>
        <blockquote>
          “A language can be imperfect and still be kind, and I think that's what makes it beautiful.”
        </blockquote>
        <p class="note">
          Pino didn't start as a serious project. It started with a girl, a humble laptop and a C++ course.
        </p>
        <p class="more"><a href="/about/">Read the story</a></p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <Image src={doodle} alt="Vincent, Re-l and Pino, drawn as small chibi figures." width={380} format="webp" quality={70} />
        <figcaption>Vincent, Re-l and Pino.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Install" id="install">
    <Fragment slot="title">Install Pino 0.4</Fragment>
    <Commands
      items={[
        { label: "Windows (PowerShell)", lang: "powershell", code: `irm ${raw}/install.ps1 | iex` },
        { label: "macOS and Linux", lang: "bash", code: `curl -fsSL ${raw}/install.sh | bash` },
      ]}
    />
    <p class="note">Then <code>pino init my-app</code> creates a project. <a href="/install/">Requirements and upgrading from 0.3</a></p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .text {
    max-width: 40rem;
    color: var(--soft);
  }
  .note {
    max-width: 36rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--soft);
  }
  .more a {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
    padding-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }
  .more a::after {
    content: " →";
  }
  .more a:hover {
    color: var(--pine);
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .status {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .status .inner {
    position: relative;
    padding-block: 1.25rem 3rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .status h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.4rem;
  }

  .why {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 15rem);
    gap: 2rem 3rem;
    align-items: end;
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 1.9rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: italic;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .why .note {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  figure {
    margin: 0;
  }
  figure img {
    display: block;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    figure img {
      filter: brightness(0.9);
    }
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--soft);
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .why {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .why figure {
      max-width: 15rem;
    }
  }
</style>
